<p>NOTES: Results for the latest quarter reflect the one-time write-off of in-process research and development of $4.5 million associated with the acquisition of Deming Software Inc and expenses of $279,000 incurred in connection with post acquisition costs related to the acquisition of Deming.</p>
<p>Without the in-process research and development charge and Deming-related integration expenses, net income and earnings per share for the fourth quarter of 1996 would have been $281,000 and 3 cents, respectively.</p>
<p>Without the Deming-related integration expenses, net loss and net loss per share for full-year 1996 would have been $461,000 and 5 cents, respectively. These results compared with total revenues, net loss and net loss per share of $6.7 million, $3.6 million and 48 cents per share, respectively, for full-year 1995.</p>
